    {
      "id": 133747,
      "name": "owlfile",
      "username": "owlfile",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/o/b5ac83/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2015-02-25T00:47:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"phantaskippy\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/48/1897_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> phantaskippy:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>In the app with RC Wraith's Sleuth power you can choose to play an environment card she has revealed, the play fails and the card is returned to the deck, but you can shoose that action instead of discard.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>good point!</p>\n<p>… Feels different to me though, that decision is \"triggered\" by the revealing of the environment card (which is linked to an activated power), it's not the first step. Con's bunker mentions nothing about not being able to reveal cards, so there is no reason one can't play \"sleuth\"while it is in play, with cons bunker it could be read as flatly environment cards cannot be played so would sugggest the option can't be taken.</p>\n<p>The end result of the wraith slueth example would always (? i think) be to discard the card regardless so it doesnt make much difference; with the con's bunker/foam grenade example it would have more of an effect (either being able to recieve the 1 hp healing with no cost, or being forced to destroy con's bunker whether you want to or not).</p>\n<p>I love this game, but it can be painful at times, as are all great love stories <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/confused.png?v=12\" title=\":confused:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":confused:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>",
      "post_number": 4,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:09:29.253Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
      "reads": 0,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 0.0,
      "yours": false,
      "topic_id": 12434,
      "topic_slug": "cons-bunker-and-adhesive-foam-grenade",
      "display_username": "owlfile",
      "primary_group_name": null,
      "flair_name": null,
      "flair_url": null,
      "flair_bg_color": null,
      "flair_color": null,
      "flair_group_id": null,
      "badges_granted": [],
      "version": 1,
      "can_edit": false,
      "can_delete": false,
      "can_recover": false,
      "can_see_hidden_post": false,
      "can_wiki": false,
      "read": false,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "[quote=\"phantaskippy\"]\n\nIn the app with RC Wraith&#39;s Sleuth power you can choose to play an environment card she has revealed, the play fails and the card is returned to the deck, but you can shoose that action instead of discard.\n\n[/quote]\n\ngood point!\n\n... Feels different to me though, that decision is &quot;triggered&quot; by the revealing of the environment card (which is linked to an activated power), it&#39;s not the first step. Con&#39;s bunker mentions nothing about not being able to reveal cards, so there is no reason one can&#39;t play &quot;sleuth&quot;while it is in play, with cons bunker it could be read as flatly environment cards cannot be played so would sugggest the option can&#39;t be taken.\n\nThe end result of the wraith slueth example would always (? i think) be to discard the card regardless so it doesnt make much difference; with the con&#39;s bunker/foam grenade example it would have more of an effect (either being able to recieve the 1 hp healing with no cost, or being forced to destroy con&#39;s bunker whether you want to or not).\n\nI love this game, but it can be painful at times, as are all great love stories :/\n",
